        // n = r + k * period for some k >= 0
        // a^n = a^(r + k * period) = a^r * (a^period)^k = a^r * 1^k = a^r (mod p)
        // So the equation becomes: (r + k * period) * a^r ≡ b (mod p)
        // => k * period * a^r ≡ (b - r * a^r) (mod p)
        // => k ≡ (b - r * a^r) * (period * a^r)^(-1) (mod p)
        // But period * a^r might not be invertible modulo p, so we need to handle this carefully

